From 86e7709e6d31cf50cccf7ebcadc516954a54c9fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:49:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/crtc: do not BUG when an out-fence is signalled while it
 is named

Since fence ops are protected by RCU, signalling a fence whose ops have
neither .release nor .wait clears fence->ops, and the CRTC out-fence is
such a fence.  dma_fence_driver_name() reads the ops once and calls
.get_driver_name through them, but fence_to_crtc() reads fence->ops a
second time and BUGs unless it still points at drm_crtc_fence_ops.  If
the vblank interrupt signals the fence between the two reads, a plain
SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO from userspace takes the kernel down:

  kernel BUG at drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c:161!
  Comm: RenderThread
   drm_crtc_fence_get_driver_name+0x2c/0x30
   sync_file_get_name+0x50/0xa0
   sync_file_ioctl+0x4a0/0x770

A NULL ops pointer in fence_to_crtc() only means the fence has been
signalled after the caller got there through our own ops.  Keep the
check for a foreign ops pointer and accept NULL; the CRTC, which holds
the fence lock the container_of() goes through, outlives its fences.

Fixes: f4cc3ab824d6 ("dma-buf: protected fence ops by RCU v8")
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
index 63ead8ba67..0c19452522 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
@@ -158,7 +158,16 @@ static const struct dma_fence_ops drm_crtc_fence_ops;
 
 static struct drm_crtc *fence_to_crtc(struct dma_fence *fence)
 {
-	BUG_ON(rcu_access_pointer(fence->ops) != &drm_crtc_fence_ops);
+	const struct dma_fence_ops *ops = rcu_access_pointer(fence->ops);
+
+	/*
+	 * Signalling clears fence->ops (dma_fence_signal_timestamp_locked()),
+	 * and it can do so between dma_fence_driver_name() reading the ops
+	 * and calling us through them. NULL here only means the fence was
+	 * signalled in that window: we were reached through our own ops, and
+	 * the CRTC outlives its fences.
+	 */
+	BUG_ON(ops && ops != &drm_crtc_fence_ops);
 	return container_of(fence->extern_lock, struct drm_crtc, fence_lock);
 }
 
